<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Lithuania (1941)</h1><p class="st-meta">1941 CE – 1941 CE · capital Kaunas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lithuanian government formed during the June Uprising of 1941, which hoped to restore independence but was dissolved by the Germans after six weeks.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> invaded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> on 22 June 1941, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-activist-front">Lithuanian Activist Front</a> launched the June Uprising against Soviet rule. On 23 June it proclaimed restored independence on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaunas">Kaunas</a> radio and formed a Provisional Government. Its intended head, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazys-skirpa">Kazys Škirpa</a>, was held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>, so <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juozas-ambrazevicius">Juozas Ambrazevičius</a> served as acting prime minister.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government tried to reverse Soviet nationalisation and re-establish Lithuanian institutions, but the Germans did not recognise it. It also issued anti-Jewish regulations while killings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> by German units and Lithuanian collaborators began, a record that remains deeply controversial.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Germans set up their own civil administration within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/reichskommissariat-ostland">Reichskommissariat Ostland</a>, and on 5 August 1941 the Provisional Government dissolved itself rather than become a German instrument. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a> remained under German occupation until 1944 and then became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lithuanian-soviet-socialist-republic">Lithuanian Soviet Socialist Republic</a> again.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-lithuania-1941.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Lithuania (1941)" width="320" height="195"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Session_of_the_Provisional_Government_of_Lithuania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1941 CE – 1941 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kaunas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Juozas Ambrazevičius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lithuanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lithuania">Lithuania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lithuanian Provisional Government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1941&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-lithuania-1941" aria-label="Provisional Government of Lithuania (1941) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5206 300 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Lithuania (1941) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5526 556L5556 562M5526 556L5520 501"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5556 562h0M5520 501h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5526 556h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5526 556h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kaunas. <a href="/atlas?year=1941&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-lithuania-1941">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
